========================================================================
PLAIN ENGLISH (RULES 1.10)
========================================================================

**What changed**
RFC-003 used to say RFC-002 string / args / walk floors were usable
on the product path (`Process.Args`, `FS.Walk`, native regex). Those
modules are not in the tree. The RFC now says they were **not**
shipped. Path-A caps and F14 net honesty are unchanged.

**Why it matters**
An audit RFC that repeats a closed RFC's false success is pride
(SINS #3). Agents would import floors that do not exist.

**What is not done**
No args parser. No directory walk. No regex product. Named-gap still
open. No push. SPRINT F19 row is Docs Writer, not this OWN.

